Read steps from sensorfw and make the other sensors optional

SailfishOS ships QtSensors 5.6: no QStepCounterSensor, no QHrmSensor. stepsource.h wraps
the step count: QtSensors as before, or sensorfw's stepcountersensor through
libsensorclient (SENSORLOGD_SENSORFW), with standby override so it counts while the display
is off. The first-reading wait runs the event loop (sensorfw delivers it as a signal).
SENSORLOGD_HEARTRATE and SENSORLOGD_BAROMETER build those loggers only where their sensors
exist. SENSORLOGD_COUNTER_RESETS_ON_OPEN handles a counter that starts from 0 when opened
(the Qualcomm Sensor Core) and one that starts over mid-run. Records carry their own time
(currentSecsSinceEpoch() is static and Qt 5.8+). QML import dir configurable.

